 environment strongly favors Democratic candidates", "All ten professional race ratings call it a Democratic flip, and prediction markets price a Democratic win near 95%", "A late-September poll reportedly showed Kiley and Pan virtually tied, the main evidence the race is closer than consensus", "Pan holds a large outside-spending edge that offsets Kiley's cash-on-hand advantage"], "rationale": "The redrawn D+5 district, a favorable Democratic midterm environment, and unanimous expert calls for a flip point to Pan unseating Kiley, and markets agree. With little public polling available and one reported survey showing a near tie, the expected margin sits below the strongest readings but still clearly on the Democratic side.", "watch": "If additional independent polls corroborate the reported tie, or Kiley's incumbency and cross-party appeal prove durable among moderates, the race could tighten toward tossup territory.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Kevin Kiley (I) is running.", "Kevin Kiley is an independent standing in for the Republican side."]}, "overview": "California's sixth district became substantially more Democratic after redistricting, and incumbent Kevin Kiley, running as an independent, faces Democrat Richard Pan, a former state senator best known for his vaccine-policy record. The seat's new D+5 lean, combined with a midterm environment that favors Democratic candidates, has led every professional race rating to call the district a Democratic flip, with most rating it Solid or Likely Democratic. Prediction markets likewise price a Democratic win near 95%.\n\nThe main counterweight is limited public polling: a late-September Sacramento-area survey reportedly showed the two candidates virtually tied, and one ratings shop places the race only at Lean Democratic. Pan also benefits from a large outside-spending advantage that offsets Kiley's fundraising edge, and Kamala Harris campaigned with Sacramento-area Democrats in early October. The forecast expects Pan to prevail by a solid but not overwhelming margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9603, "margin": 11.77}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.95, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9719, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9738, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9473, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9501, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9607, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9617, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9576, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.8238, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.8267, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.8267, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.911, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9123, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.8963, "margin": 9.5}]}